        "id": "R-migration-1",
        "line": 11,
        "location": "src/api.rs:6",
        "raisedBy": [
          "migration"
        ],
        "recommendation": "Remove `#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]` so `order_id`, `customer_id`, `total_cents` and `status` keep their snake_case names and only `currency` is added. Today `GET /orders/{id}` returns `order_id`, `customer_id` and `total_cents`; after this change it returns `orderId`, `customerId` and `totalCents`, so every partner integration reading those fields gets a missing field on the first response after deploy. `docs/api.md` promises that \"a field is never renamed or removed without two releases of deprecation\", the proposal only announces an added field, and the release note has no **BREAKING** item. If camelCase is wanted, it needs its own change: emit both names for two releases, then mark the removal BREAKING.",
        "reported": true,
        "role": "migration",
        "severity": "high",
        "status": "open",
        "step": "code.review",
        "title": "camelCase renames every existing order JSON field"
      },
