        "awaiting": "author",
        "confidence": "high",
        "evidence": "pub default_currency: String,\n",
        "history": [
          {
            "by": "migration",
            "note": null,
            "ref": null,
            "status": "open",
            "to": null
          }
        ],
        "id": "R-migration-2",
        "line": 35,
        "location": "src/config.rs:10",
        "raisedBy": [
          "migration"
        ],
        "recommendation": "Give the field a default — `#[serde(default = \"...\")]` returning `\"EUR\"`, the currency every existing order is in — so a deployed `config.toml` holding only `database_url` and `listen` keeps loading. As written, `toml::from_str` fails with a missing-field error on such a file and the service refuses to start after the upgrade; neither the release note nor the docs tell operators to add the key. If the key must stay required, announce it as a **BREAKING** item in the release note with the line to add, and add a test that loads the pre-change `config.example.toml`.",
        "reported": true,
        "role": "migration",
        "severity": "high",
        "status": "open",
